{"id":"temple-of-vespasian-and-titus","name":"Temple of Vespasian and Titus","qid":"Q731284","country":"Italy","locality":"Rome","lat":"41.892727777","lon":"12.483891666","built":"79","year":79,"year_text":"79","century":"1st century","era":"Ancient world","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"","heritage":"","type":"temple; Roman temple","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Vespasian_and_Titus","text":"The so-called Temple of Vespasian and Titus (Latin: Templum divi Vespasiani, Italian: Tempio di Vespasiano) is located in Rome at the western end of the Roman Forum between the Temple of Concordia and the Temple of Saturn. It was dedicated to the deified Vespasian. It was begun by Titus in 79 after Vespasian's death and Titus's succession.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple_of_Vespasian_and_Titus","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-34bf155d0db6","w":1200,"h":900,"title":"Forum temple of vespasian.jpg","o":"gh-34bf155d0db6.jpg","credit":{"text":"Anthony M. from Rome, Italy","license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Forum_temple_of_vespasian.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"assassins-creed-brotherhood--tempio-di-vespasiano","game":"assassins-creed-brotherhood","name":"Tempio di Vespasiano","verified":false,"text":"","text_source":"","text_license":"","images":[{"id":"gh-p751c4843d54","w":512,"h":256,"o":"gh-p751c4843d54.png","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Assassin's Creed Brotherhood, © the game's publisher.","source":"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/File:Tempio_di_Vespasiano.png","via":"Fandom (assassinscreed)","note":"Fandom upload by Vatsa1708 on 2012-09-23"}}]}]}